{"kind":"request","text":"MT-1: a deterministic in-memory transport for the recorded client. Hugh, 21 November, from the map application: its demo and most model tests run a separate engine, while hosted mode uses dap's ScopeClient. An application must run demo, tests and hosted mode through one client, and keep no second engine.\nAdd to the client package's testing entry a memory transport that implements the client's transport interface over the derive testing Ledger: the declared handle, signed identity with an authorization policy the test supplies, exact settle and exact-repeat receipts, bounded reads and paging that match the room's, and observation that advances by itself after each commit. Deterministic clock, no timers of its own. Reuse the Ledger, the request fixture (packages/client/test/request-support.ts) and the client memory stores; build no second judge. Real enrollment and sessions stay outside it.\nWitness: the existing client request and replica tests run on it in place of their hand-written partial service, with fewer lines; one test submits, loses the reply after commit, repeats, and observes the change. Document it in the developer guide where an application author sets up tests.\nReadback: fc65bfa5. A single head with its gate, in the developer group or after it. No live scope in this head; a live memory transport is a later request after PB-3.","body":{"conditions":"Gate END on the exact head; checker approval; the existing client tests moved onto the transport; the developer guide section.","target_head":"95ec0456526857a6e1fd598ef2ede6aea4a79259","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}